1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,202
A members area is a part of your site that only approved, signed-in people can open.

2
00:00:06,202 --> 00:00:10,537
In this video, you let visitors register, give them a role, and limit

3
00:00:10,537 --> 00:00:12,040
a page to that role.

4
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,708
A members area has three parts:

5
00:00:18,708 --> 00:00:23,628
registration lets visitors create their own accounts, a role groups the people who

6
00:00:23,628 --> 00:00:28,380
share the same access, and permissions decide which content each role can open.

7
00:00:29,130 --> 00:00:31,555
Two of the system roles matter here.

8
00:00:31,555 --> 00:00:37,618
Anonymous covers visitors who are not signed in, and its permissions also apply to signed-in users.

9
00:00:37,618 --> 00:00:40,390
Authenticated covers every signed-in user.

10
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:46,194
Both roles start with the permission View all content, so every page is public.

11
00:00:46,194 --> 00:00:50,712
To limit a page, you remove that permission from both roles, and grant

12
00:00:50,712 --> 00:00:54,220
the page's type to a role you create, such as Member.

13
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:57,007
The video follows four stages.

14
00:00:57,007 --> 00:01:01,478
You enable registration, make a content type securable so it gets its own

15
00:01:01,478 --> 00:01:06,119
permissions, create the Member role, close that type to visitors, and try it

16
00:01:06,119 --> 00:01:07,930
with a page and a sign-up.

17
00:01:12,230 --> 00:01:14,861
Registration is a feature of its own.

18
00:01:14,861 --> 00:01:19,940
Open Tools, Features, search for registration, and enable Users Registration.

19
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:24,040
The page reloads with a message that the feature was enabled.

20
00:01:24,498 --> 00:01:29,792
The feature adds a page under Settings, Security, Registration, with three options.

21
00:01:29,792 --> 00:01:34,730
Users must verify their email address makes people confirm it by email, which

22
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:37,288
requires a configured email provider.

23
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:41,936
Use site theme for registration page shows the form in your site theme.

24
00:01:41,936 --> 00:01:46,383
Users must be approved before they can log in leaves each registered account

25
00:01:46,383 --> 00:01:49,040
disabled until an administrator enables it.

26
00:01:49,495 --> 00:01:53,500
For a members area, approval keeps the decision in your hands.

27
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:58,271
Let's select Users must be approved before they can log in, and click Save.

28
00:01:58,271 --> 00:02:02,335
Visitors reach the Register page from a link on the login page.

29
00:02:06,635 --> 00:02:10,175
A page is members-only because of its content type.

30
00:02:10,175 --> 00:02:16,821
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, this site has two page types, Page and Members Page.

31
00:02:16,821 --> 00:02:18,685
Let's edit Members Page.

32
00:02:19,195 --> 00:02:23,781
Securable determines whether a content type can have custom permissions.

33
00:02:23,781 --> 00:02:25,663
Page is already securable.

34
00:02:25,663 --> 00:02:29,603
Members Page is not, so it has no permissions of its own, and

35
00:02:29,603 --> 00:02:33,425
View all content opens its pages for everyone who holds it.

36
00:02:33,879 --> 00:02:36,260
Let's select Securable, and click Save.

37
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:40,440
The content type gets its own permissions, which the role editor lists in

38
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:41,869
a group of their own.

39
00:02:46,169 --> 00:02:50,192
Open Access Control, Roles, which lists the roles of the site.

40
00:02:50,192 --> 00:02:54,097
The system roles carry a System badge and cannot be deleted.

41
00:02:54,097 --> 00:02:55,339
Click Add Role.

42
00:02:55,798 --> 00:03:00,478
Enter Member as the name, add a description, and click Save & Configure.

43
00:03:00,478 --> 00:03:03,598
The role is created, and its permissions open.

44
00:03:04,052 --> 00:03:06,709
The editor lists every permission as a row.

45
00:03:06,709 --> 00:03:10,939
Search for Members Page, and the permissions of the type appear in their

46
00:03:10,939 --> 00:03:14,302
own group, with an Allow column and an Effective column.

47
00:03:14,772 --> 00:03:19,243
Select View Members Page by others in the Allow column, and click Save.

48
00:03:19,243 --> 00:03:21,682
Members can open pages of this type.

49
00:03:25,982 --> 00:03:31,657
Anonymous and Authenticated both hold View all content, which opens every page.

50
00:03:31,657 --> 00:03:34,862
Edit Anonymous first, and search for view.

51
00:03:35,313 --> 00:03:40,325
A type that is not securable has no permission of its own to grant back.

52
00:03:40,325 --> 00:03:45,787
Make every type that visitors read securable before you clear View all content.

53
00:03:45,787 --> 00:03:47,843
Page is already securable.

54
00:03:48,341 --> 00:03:52,961
Clear View all content, select View Page by others so visitors keep the

55
00:03:52,961 --> 00:03:55,061
public pages, and click Save.

56
00:03:55,546 --> 00:03:59,788
Edit Authenticated next, clear View all content, and click Save.

57
00:03:59,788 --> 00:04:03,304
Signed-in users keep reading Page through Anonymous.

58
00:04:03,304 --> 00:04:08,395
Members Page opens for the Member role, for administrators, and for roles that

59
00:04:08,395 --> 00:04:11,486
hold Edit content for others, such as Editor.

60
00:04:15,786 --> 00:04:19,764
Pages of this type are created like any other content.

61
00:04:19,764 --> 00:04:24,406
Open Content, Content Items, click New, and choose Members Page.

62
00:04:24,867 --> 00:04:28,944
Enter the title Members Lounge, and the permalink members-lounge.

63
00:04:28,944 --> 00:04:33,077
Add a line of text for members, so the page has something to show.

64
00:04:33,531 --> 00:04:34,655
Click Publish.

65
00:04:34,655 --> 00:04:36,960
The page has no setting of its own.

66
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:41,064
It is members-only because its type is, and every page of that type

67
00:04:41,064 --> 00:04:43,031
follows the same permissions.

68
00:04:47,331 --> 00:04:52,119
A visitor reads the public home page, which anyone can open without signing

69
00:04:52,119 --> 00:04:55,251
in, and follows its link to the members lounge.

70
00:04:55,714 --> 00:05:00,097
The visitor cannot view the page, so the site asks them to log in.

71
00:05:00,097 --> 00:05:03,324
The login page links to Register as a new user.

72
00:05:03,777 --> 00:05:08,927
The form asks for a username, an email address, and a password, entered twice.

73
00:05:08,927 --> 00:05:13,157
Let's enter the details of a future member, and click Register.

74
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:23,523
Because approval is on, the account is created but cannot be used until it is approved.

75
00:05:23,523 --> 00:05:26,943
A page titled User Registration Pending says so.

76
00:05:31,243 --> 00:05:34,768
As an administrator, open Access Control, Users.

77
00:05:34,768 --> 00:05:38,033
The account is listed with a Disabled badge.

78
00:05:38,491 --> 00:05:42,940
Open the account's Actions menu, choose Enable, and confirm with Ok.

79
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:49,071
The list reloads with a message that the account was enabled, and the Disabled badge disappears.

80
00:05:49,524 --> 00:05:55,497
Registration does not assign a role, so click Edit, select Member under Roles, and click Save.

81
00:05:55,497 --> 00:05:58,184
The account belongs to the Member role.

82
00:05:58,635 --> 00:06:02,165
Other sign-ups wait in the same list until you enable them.

83
00:06:02,165 --> 00:06:06,075
To stop someone signing in later, choose Disable in the same menu.

84
00:06:10,375 --> 00:06:14,558
The member opens the members lounge from the home page, and logs in

85
00:06:14,558 --> 00:06:17,995
with the username and password chosen at registration.

86
00:06:17,995 --> 00:06:22,235
The login page asks for a username or email address, and a password.

87
00:06:22,689 --> 00:06:26,663
After logging in, the site returns to the page the member asked for,

88
00:06:26,663 --> 00:06:28,542
and the members lounge opens.

89
00:06:28,542 --> 00:06:31,979
Visitors who are not signed in are sent to the login page.

90
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:35,277
The public pages stay open to everyone.

91
00:06:35,277 --> 00:06:40,210
Only the pages of a type that you secure and restrict ask for a sign-in.

92
00:06:44,410 --> 00:06:48,370
Visitors can also sign in with an account they already have.

93
00:06:48,370 --> 00:06:54,130
Google Authentication, GitHub Authentication and Meta Login are features of their own, and

94
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:57,970
each adds a page under Settings, Security, Authentication.

95
00:06:57,970 --> 00:07:00,610
A separate video covers each provider.

96
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:08,587
With Users Registration enabled, accounts created this way follow the same Registration settings, including approval.

97
00:07:08,587 --> 00:07:13,522
Once one of these features is enabled, the Registration page gains an External

98
00:07:13,522 --> 00:07:19,220
Authentication tab, where Disable new external registration closes sign-ups from providers.

99
00:07:21,220 --> 00:07:26,005
A members area combines registration, a role, and a securable content type.

100
00:07:26,005 --> 00:07:31,026
Remove View all content from Anonymous and Authenticated, grant the type to the

101
00:07:31,026 --> 00:07:33,625
Member role, and approve each sign-up.

102
00:07:33,625 --> 00:07:35,160
Thanks for watching.

